This adaptation replaces the original worker service with the open source Pi CLI.
The Claude Code plugin name and its hook, script, and skill design are retained.

Modified files include the plugin manifest, README, hook messages, worker scripts,
shared transport, skills, and evaluation runner. They add Pi configuration,
stdin prompts, checked JSON responses, controlled target writes, multiple
reference files, and Pi transport checks. Original service setup and benchmark
claims were removed from the adapted documentation.

The worker and hook shell scripts use .sh file extensions.

The workers and benchmark use native Bash and jq. The shared Bash helper
checks Pi responses and cleans up worker processes. No Python runtime is needed.

The plugin also supplies native Pi settings in .pi/settings.json. Worker
processes load these settings from the plugin directory. Caller file paths
and the existing global Pi authentication directory keep their meaning.

Spotify is the original author. This Pi adaptation is not an official Spotify
release. The manifest retains the original author and source repository.
